# One RPN block in, LaTeX out. See README.md for the format.

## the quadratic formula
rpn: b neg b 2 ^ 4ac - sqrt + 2a /
latex: \frac{-b + \sqrt{b^{2} - 4 a c}}{2 a}

# The bracket rule

## a looser left child gets brackets
rpn: a b + c *
latex: (a + b) c

## a looser right child gets brackets
rpn: c a b + *
latex: c (a + b)

## a sum as the base of a power gets brackets
rpn: a b + 2 ^
latex: (a + b)^{2}

## an equal-rank right child of - gets brackets
rpn: a b c - -
latex: a - (b - c)

## a sum as the right child of - gets brackets
rpn: a b c + -
latex: a - (b + c)

## an equal-rank right child of + needs none
rpn: a b c + +
latex: a + b + c

## a difference as the right child of + needs none
rpn: a b c - +
latex: a + b - c

## a left-nested difference needs none
rpn: a b - c -
latex: a - b - c

## a fraction boxes its parts
rpn: a b + c d - /
latex: \frac{a + b}{c - d}

## an exponent is boxed
rpn: x a b + ^
latex: x^{a + b}

## a square root is boxed
rpn: a b + sqrt
latex: \sqrt{a + b}

## a subscript is boxed
rpn: x i 1 + ssc
latex: x_{i + 1}

## tall contents get stretchy brackets
rpn: a b / c + 2 ^
latex: \left(\frac{a}{b} + c\right)^{2}

# Powers and subscripts

## a subscripted base of a power needs no brackets
rpn: x i ssc 2 ^
latex: x_{i}^{2}

## a glued subscript as the base of a power
rpn: x1 2 ^
latex: x_{1}^{2}

## a power as the base of a power gets brackets
rpn: a 2 ^ 3 ^
latex: (a^{2})^{3}

## a power is subscripted without brackets
rpn: x 2 ^ i ssc
latex: x^{2}_{i}

## tensor indices
rpn: T a ^ b ssc
latex: T^{a}_{b}

## a subscripted subscript is grouped invisibly
rpn: x i ssc j ssc
latex: {x_{i}}_{j}

## a subscripted sum is grouped invisibly
rpn: a b + i ssc
latex: {a + b}_{i}

## a subscripted power of a subscript is grouped invisibly
rpn: x i ssc 2 ^ j ssc
latex: {x_{i}^{2}}_{j}

## _ is another spelling of ssc
rpn: x i _
latex: x_{i}

## _ and ^ together, tensor style
rpn: T a ^ b _
latex: T^{a}_{b}

## _ is grouped invisibly like ssc
rpn: x i _ j _
latex: {x_{i}}_{j}

## stack underflow names _ as written
rpn: x _
error: `_` needs 2 values, but only 1 is available

## _ glued to its operands
rpn: x_i
error: `x_i` needs spaces: tokens are separated by whitespace

# Multiplication

## glued factors print side by side
rpn: 4ac
latex: 4 a c

## * prints side by side
rpn: 2 a *
latex: 2 a

## a number glued to a reserved value
rpn: 2pi
latex: 2 \pi

## bracketed factors print side by side
rpn: a b + c d + *
latex: (a + b) (c + d)

## two numbers get \cdot
rpn: 2 3 *
latex: 2 \cdot 3

## a number after a letter gets \cdot
rpn: a 2 *
latex: a \cdot 2

## a number after a power gets \cdot
rpn: x 2 ^ 3 *
latex: x^{2} \cdot 3

# Functions, negation and logic

## an atom argument needs no brackets
rpn: x sin
latex: \sin x

## a subscripted atom argument needs no brackets
rpn: x1 sin
latex: \sin x_{1}

## a sum argument gets brackets
rpn: x y + sin
latex: \sin (x + y)

## a product argument gets brackets
rpn: 2x sin
latex: \sin (2 x)

## a function followed by a factor gets brackets
rpn: x sin y *
latex: (\sin x) y

## a function as the last factor needs none
rpn: y x sin *
latex: y \sin x

## a function in the middle of a product gets brackets
rpn: y x sin * z *
latex: y (\sin x) z

## two functions side by side
rpn: x sin y sin *
latex: (\sin x) \sin y

## a sum as the last factor needs none
rpn: c n a n ssc sum *
latex: c \sum_{n} a_{n}

## a negation after + gets brackets
rpn: a b neg +
latex: a + (-b)

## a negation before + needs none
rpn: b neg a +
latex: -b + a

## a negation after = needs none
rpn: a b neg =
latex: a = -b

## a negated sum gets brackets
rpn: a b + neg
latex: -(a + b)

## and binds looser than relations
rpn: a b = c d = and
latex: a = b \wedge c = d

## or binds looser than and
rpn: a b or c and
latex: (a \vee b) \wedge c

## and and or under a relation get brackets
rpn: a b or c d and =
latex: (a \vee b) = (c \wedge d)

## exists
rpn: x exists
latex: \exists x

## forall
rpn: x forall
latex: \forall x

# Relations

## ASCII relations
rpn: a b < c d > and
latex: a < b \wedge c > d

## <= is \leq, >= is \geq, != is \neq
rpn: a b <= c d >= and e f != and
latex: a \leq b \wedge c \geq d \wedge e \neq f

## much less and much greater
rpn: a b << c d >> and
latex: a \ll b \wedge c \gg d

## -> is \to
rpn: x 0 ->
latex: x \to 0

## relations by name
rpn: a b leq c d approx and e f equiv and
latex: a \leq b \wedge c \approx d \wedge e \equiv f

## more relations by name
rpn: a b sim c d propto and
latex: a \sim b \wedge c \propto d

## set relations
rpn: x reals in A B subseteq and
latex: x \in \mathbb{R} \wedge A \subseteq B

## not in, subset
rpn: x A notin A B subset and
latex: x \notin A \wedge A \subset B

## supset
rpn: A B supset
latex: A \supset B

## mapsto
rpn: x x 2 ^ mapsto
latex: x \mapsto x^{2}

## perp
rpn: u v perp
latex: u \perp v

## a chain of mixed relations
rpn: 0 x < 1 <=
latex: 0 < x \leq 1

## relations bind looser than arithmetic
rpn: a b + c d * <=
latex: a + b \leq c d

## in is a reserved word, not a product
rpn: in
error: `in` needs 2 values, but none is available

# Logical arrows

## => is \implies
rpn: x 0 > x 2 ^ 0 > =>
latex: x > 0 \implies x^{2} > 0

## <=> is \iff
rpn: p q <=>
latex: p \iff q

## arrows by name
rpn: p q implies q p impliedby iff
latex: p \implies q \iff q \impliedby p

## arrows bind looser than and and or
rpn: p q and r or s =>
latex: p \wedge q \vee r \implies s

## iff binds looser than implies
rpn: p q => r <=>
latex: p \implies q \iff r

## an arrow under and gets brackets
rpn: p q => r and
latex: (p \implies q) \wedge r

## an arrow chain is bracketed on the left
rpn: p q => r =>
latex: (p \implies q) \implies r

## an arrow chain is bracketed on the right
rpn: p q r => =>
latex: p \implies (q \implies r)

# Logical not

## not
rpn: p not
latex: \neg p

## not binds tighter than and
rpn: p not q and
latex: \neg p \wedge q

## not of a conjunction gets brackets
rpn: p q and not
latex: \neg (p \wedge q)

## not of a relation gets brackets
rpn: a b = not
latex: \neg (a = b)

## not of a quantifier needs none
rpn: x exists not
latex: \neg \exists x

# Factorial

## factorial
rpn: n !
latex: n!

## factorial of a sum gets brackets
rpn: n 1 + !
latex: (n + 1)!

## factorial of a product gets brackets
rpn: 2n !
latex: (2 n)!

## factorial of a subscripted atom
rpn: n1 !
latex: n_{1}!

## factorial of a factorial
rpn: n ! !
latex: (n!)!

## a power of a factorial
rpn: n ! 2 ^
latex: (n!)^{2}

## factorials in a fraction
rpn: n ! k ! n k - ! * /
latex: \frac{n!}{k! (n - k)!}

## a factorial after a number gets \cdot
rpn: 2 n ! *
latex: 2 n!

## infty is infinity
rpn: x infty ->
latex: x \to \infty

## oo is no longer reserved
rpn: oo
latex: o o

# Accents

## a dot is a time derivative
rpn: x dot
latex: \dot{x}

## two dots are a second derivative
rpn: x ddot
latex: \ddot{x}

## Newton's second law for a spring
rpn: m x ddot * k x * neg =
latex: m \ddot{x} = -k x

## a dotted letter is an atom as the base of a power
rpn: x dot 2 ^
latex: \dot{x}^{2}

## a dotted letter is an atom as a function's argument
rpn: x dot sin
latex: \sin \dot{x}

## a dotted letter takes a subscript directly
rpn: x dot i ssc
latex: \dot{x}_{i}

## an accent covers its whole argument, without brackets
rpn: x y + dot
latex: \dot{x + y}

## an accent over a sum isn't an atom
rpn: x y + dot 2 ^
latex: (\dot{x + y})^{2}

## a line can't break inside an accent
rpn: x y + br dot
layout: multline
error: `br` can't break a line inside an accent

# Sums and integrals

## a series
rpn: n 1 = infty 1 n 2 ^ / ser
latex: \sum_{n = 1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{n^{2}}

## a summand that is a sum gets brackets
rpn: n a n ssc b + sum
latex: \sum_{n} (a_{n} + b)

## an integral writes the d and its spacing
rpn: 0 pi x sin x int
latex: \int_{0}^{\pi} \sin x \,dx

# Limits, max and min, sup and inf

## a limit
rpn: x 0 -> x sin x / lim
latex: \lim_{x \to 0} \frac{\sin x}{x}

## a limit at infinity
rpn: n infty -> a n _ lim
latex: \lim_{n \to \infty} a_{n}

## a limit of a sum gets brackets
rpn: x 0 -> f g + lim
latex: \lim_{x \to 0} (f + g)

## liminf and limsup
rpn: n infty -> a n _ liminf n infty -> a n _ limsup <=
latex: \liminf_{n \to \infty} a_{n} \leq \limsup_{n \to \infty} a_{n}

## max over a set
rpn: x S in f max
latex: \max_{x \in S} f

## min over a set
rpn: x S in f min
latex: \min_{x \in S} f

## argmax and argmin
rpn: x f argmax x f argmin !=
latex: \operatorname*{arg\,max}_{x} f \neq \operatorname*{arg\,min}_{x} f

## sup of a set
rpn: A sup
latex: \sup A

## inf of a set
rpn: A inf
latex: \inf A

## sup of a sum gets brackets
rpn: A B + sup
latex: \sup (A + B)

## inf is not infty
rpn: A inf infty <
latex: \inf A < \infty

## a break inside a limit's subscript
layout: multline
rpn: x a b + br -> f lim
error: `br` can't break a line inside a subscript

# Variadic operators

## a matrix
rpn: [ a b ; c d mat
latex: \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}

## a column vector
rpn: [ a b c col
latex: \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \\ c \end{pmatrix}

## cases
rpn: [ 1 x 0 = ; 0 "otherwise" cases
latex: \begin{cases} 1 & x = 0 \\ 0 & \text{otherwise} \end{cases}

## a fixed-arity operator inside a row
rpn: [ n a n ssc sum x ; c d mat
latex: \begin{pmatrix} \sum_{n} a_{n} & x \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}

## nested marks
rpn: [ [ a b col c ; d e mat
latex: \begin{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix} & c \\ d & e \end{pmatrix}

# Values

## a borrowed Greek capital is upright
rpn: Alpha
latex: \mathrm{A}

## raw LaTeX as a value
rpn: \mathcal{F} x ssc
latex: \mathcal{F}_{x}

## a raw operator
rpn: a b \overset/2
latex: \overset{a}{b}

## quoted text
rpn: "if "
latex: \text{if }

## a quote inside text
rpn: "say \"hi\""
latex: \text{say "hi"}

## a backslash inside text is kept
rpn: "costs \$5"
latex: \text{costs \$5}

# Equations

## each equation keeps its label and \notag
rpn: \label{eq:e} E m c 2 ^ * = ; a b = \notag
latex: E = m c^{2} \label{eq:e}
latex: a = b \notag

## leftovers are set side by side, with a warning
rpn: 2 x 2 ^
latex: 2 x^{2}
warning: 2 values were left on the stack, so they're set side by side; is an operator missing?

# Aligned layout (align)

## & goes before the relation
layout: aligned
rpn: a b =
latex: a &= b

## & before the relation, with a product on the right
layout: aligned
rpn: E m c 2 ^ * =
latex: E &= m c^{2}

## both sides get the same brackets as without align
layout: aligned
rpn: a b or c d and =
latex: (a \vee b) &= (c \wedge d)

## a relation on the right of a relation
layout: aligned
rpn: a b c = =
latex: a &= (b = c)

## a chain aligns at its first relation
layout: aligned
rpn: a b = c =
latex: a &= b = c

## no & without a relation at the root
layout: aligned
rpn: a b +
latex: a + b

## & goes before any relation
layout: aligned
rpn: f x g * <=
latex: f &\leq x g

## a chain of mixed relations aligns at its first
layout: aligned
rpn: a b <= c <
latex: a &\leq b < c

## an arrow at the root is where it aligns
layout: aligned
rpn: a b = c d = =>
latex: a = b &\implies c = d

## br before a relation starts its line with &
layout: aligned
rpn: x a <= b < br
latex: x &\leq a \notag \\ &< b

## br before an arrow starts its line with &
layout: aligned
rpn: a b = c d = => br
latex: a = b \notag \\ &\implies c = d

## an arrow chain aligns at its root, outside the brackets
layout: aligned
rpn: p q => r =>
latex: (p \implies q) &\implies r

## no & when the root is a logical operator
layout: aligned
rpn: a b = c d = and
latex: a = b \wedge c = d

## the label and \notag come after
layout: aligned
rpn: \label{eq:e} E m c 2 ^ * =
latex: E &= m c^{2} \label{eq:e}

## \notag after an aligned equation
layout: aligned
rpn: a b = \notag
latex: a &= b \notag

# Line breaks

## multline breaks before the operator
layout: multline
rpn: a b + c + br
latex: a + b \\ + c

## align breaks a chain at its relations
layout: aligned
rpn: a b = c = br
latex: a &= b \notag \\ &= c

## align indents a line that continues at +
layout: aligned
rpn: a b c + d + br =
latex: a &= b + c \notag \\ &\qquad + d

## a broken equation is numbered once, on its last line
layout: lines
rpn: \label{eq:x} a b + c + br
latex: a + b \notag \\ + c \label{eq:x}

## a break between factors
layout: multline
rpn: a b * br
latex: a \\ b

## a break before a number factor keeps \cdot
layout: multline
rpn: a 2 * br
latex: a \\ \cdot 2

## brackets split across a break
layout: multline
rpn: a b c + br *
latex: a \left(\vphantom{b + c} b\right. \\ \left.\vphantom{b + c} + c\right)

## split brackets in align
layout: aligned
rpn: x a b c + br * =
latex: x &= a \left(\vphantom{b + c} b\right. \notag \\ &\qquad \left.\vphantom{b + c} + c\right)

## a break in a one-line display
rpn: a b + br
error: `br` needs a display that can hold several lines, like multline, align or gather

## a break inside a fraction
layout: multline
rpn: a b + br c /
error: `br` can't break a line inside a fraction

## a break inside a square root
layout: multline
rpn: a b + br sqrt
error: `br` can't break a line inside a square root

# Lexer errors

## a number glued to an operator
rpn: 2sqrt
error: `2` is glued to the operator `sqrt`; did you mean `2 sqrt`?

## a subscript on an operator
rpn: sqrt2
error: the operator `sqrt` can't take a subscript; did you mean `2 sqrt`?

## letters after a glued subscript
rpn: x1y
error: `x1y`: glued digits after letters are a subscript and must end the token (`x1` → x₁)

## tokens need whitespace between them
rpn: 4ac-
error: `4ac-` needs spaces: tokens are separated by whitespace

## a symbol not in the language
rpn: =<
error: unknown symbol `=<`

## a relation glued to its operands
rpn: a<b
error: `a<b` needs spaces: tokens are separated by whitespace

## a label split by a space
rpn: \label{eq: energy}
error: a label is written `\label{name}`, with no spaces in the name
error: unknown symbol `energy}`

## a lone backslash
rpn: \
error: a lone `\` is not a LaTeX command

## a string with no closing quote
rpn: x "if
error: unterminated string: missing the closing "

## a string glued to the next token
rpn: "if"x
error: a string must be followed by a space

## every bad token is reported
rpn: x1y a 2sqrt b
error: `x1y`: glued digits after letters are a subscript and must end the token (`x1` → x₁)
error: `2` is glued to the operator `sqrt`; did you mean `2 sqrt`?

# Parser errors

## stack underflow
rpn: a +
error: `+` needs 2 values, but only 1 is available

## stack underflow with nothing on the stack
rpn: sqrt
error: `sqrt` needs 1 value, but none is available

## stack underflow for a raw operator
rpn: a \overset/2
error: `\overset` needs 2 values, but only 1 is available

## a raw operator takes at most 9 values, as a LaTeX command does
rpn: a b \foo/10
error: `\foo/10`: a LaTeX command takes at most 9 arguments

## a raw operator's arity can be written with leading zeros
rpn: a b \overset/02
latex: \overset{a}{b}

## a variadic operator with no mark
rpn: a b mat
error: `mat` needs a mark `[` before its entries

## a mark that's never used
rpn: [ a b
error: this mark `[` is never used by a variadic operator (`mat`, `cases`, `col`)

## an empty row
rpn: [ a ; mat
error: `mat` has an empty row

## an operator can't reach past a mark
rpn: a [ b + mat
error: `+` needs 2 values, but only 1 is available after the last `[`

## an operator can't reach past a row
rpn: [ a ; b + mat
error: `+` needs 2 values, but only 1 is available in this row

## br after a value
rpn: a br
error: `br` must come right after an operator written between its operands, such as + or =

## br after a power
rpn: a b ^ br
error: `br` must come right after an operator written between its operands, such as + or =

## br not right after its operator
rpn: a b + c br
error: `br` must come right after an operator written between its operands, such as + or =

## a second label on one equation
rpn: \label{a} x \label{b}
error: this equation already has the label `a`

## an empty block
rpn:
error: the RPN block is empty

## an empty equation before a ;
rpn: ; a
error: this equation is empty

## a trailing ;
rpn: a ;
error: nothing follows this `;`

## an operator whose arity isn't decided
rpn: a b gcd
error: `gcd` is reserved, but how many values it takes isn't decided yet

## lim needs an approach and a body
rpn: f lim
error: `lim` needs 2 values, but only 1 is available
